Building the mosh-webrtc .deb
-----------------------------

The package builds libdatachannel statically from the third_party/libdatachannel
submodule, so the source tree must have been cloned with --recurse-submodules
(or `git submodule update --init --recursive` run afterwards). The build itself
needs no network. To build in a clean Debian trixie container and collect the
artefacts in $OUT:

    OUT=/path/to/output; mkdir -p "$OUT"
    docker run --rm -v "$PWD":/src:ro -v "$OUT":/out debian:trixie sh -euc '
        apt-get update && apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
            build-essential devscripts equivs
        cp -a /src /build && cd /build
        mk-build-deps -i -r -t "apt-get -y --no-install-recommends" debian/control
        dpkg-buildpackage -us -uc -b
        cp ../mosh-webrtc_* /out/'
